<%# How the session went, written from the gym floor. #452.

    `workouts.note` has existed since #310 and the only way to write one was the workout edit
    form, which is a different page reached by leaving the session. So the note this column
    exists for -- "bar felt slow today, slept badly" -- had to survive the walk to another
    screen and a lifter remembering to take it. It is the context that explains an RPE three
    weeks later, and it is worth nothing if it is not written within a minute of the set that
    prompted it.

    Collapsed by default, and that is the whole of why it can sit on this screen at all. The
    session view is read at arm's length between sets and every pixel above the lift panels is
    a pixel of training pushed off the phone. A summary is one line; a textarea is six.

    Open when there is already a note, because a note you cannot see is a note you will write
    twice -- and because the second visit is usually to add to it rather than to start one.

    Its own htmx target, so saving swaps this block and nothing else. Posting through the
    session body instead would re-render every lift panel, which closes any <details> the
    lifter had open and scrolls the horizontal lift strip back to the start -- and they are
    standing in front of a rack with a bar loaded. %>
<div id="session-note" class="mt-4">
  <details class="group" <%= 'open' if @workout.note %>>
    <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center text-sm text-gray-500">
      <%== render('_chevron') %>
      <%# The word changes with the state because the control is doing two different jobs:
          offering to capture something, or showing what was captured. "Add a note" over an
          existing note reads as though the one below it is not there. %>
      <%= @workout.note ? 'Session note' : 'Add a note' %>
    </summary>
    <form action="/workouts/<%= @workout.id %>/session/note" method="post"
          hx-post="/workouts/<%= @workout.id %>/session/note"
          hx-target="#session-note" hx-swap="outerHTML" class="mt-2">
      <%== csrf_tag("/workouts/#{@workout.id}/session/note") %>
      <label for="session-note-text" class="sr-only">How this session went</label>
      <%# The closing tag butts against the value for the reason views/exercises/_form.erb
          gives about its own: a textarea renders every character between the tags, so a
          newline before </textarea> is a newline in the note, and it compounds on every save.

          rows="3" rather than more: three lines is a sentence or two, which is what this is
          for. A note long enough to need scrolling belongs on the record page, where there is
          room to read it back. %>
      <textarea name="note" id="session-note-text" rows="3"
                class="<%= field_style %> block min-h-11 w-full py-1.5 text-base text-gray-900 placeholder:text-gray-400"
                placeholder="Bar felt slow today, slept badly."><%= @workout.note %></textarea>
      <div class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-3">
        <button type="submit"
                class="<%= button_style %> min-h-11 bg-lime-500 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 hover:bg-lime-600">
          Save note
        </button>
        <%# Said only after a save, and only when something is stored. A blank textarea with
            "Saved" under it would be reporting on a note that was just cleared, which is
            true and reads as a failure. %>
        <%- if @saved && @workout.note %>
          <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Saved.</span>
        <%- end %>
      </div>
    </form>
  </details>
</div>
